    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d970">

                <pb facs="1044" n="1032" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg1032"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/9–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alexander C. Kirk,
                        Political Adviser to the Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean Theater, to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-02T15:00:00+02:00">September 2,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3489. Our British colleague has shown us a copy of draft peace treaty with Italy
                    prepared by FornOff.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d970-f1"/> We assume Department has
                    seen this document which in length is reminiscent of Treaty of Versailles. Quick
                    survey thereof indicates that it is very severe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d970-f1" n="38" xml:id="d970-f1-content">
                <p>See memorandum by the United Kingdom Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                    Ministers (C.F.M. (45) 3), dated September 12, 1945, <ref
                        target="frus1945v02#pg_135">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        135</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
